WEBVTT

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:02.480
Both of you, stop!

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:06.490
Mr. Masaru!

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:12.450
For yourself... right?

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.830
That's right. It's for myself.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:30.300
Before dawn, when the stars paint the sky

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:35.180
I am searching for the thing I lost

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:39.940
With a restless heart
Under the sun yet in the dark

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:44.480
I patch together little prayers
to light my path

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:49.240
I don't need anything,
as my hands are full

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:54.030
My hands are full of emptiness

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:58.870
Please, just once, nod for me

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:03.670
Just once, reach out to me like the mirror

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:08.550
I will live for that single moment,
that single second

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:12.970
All the rest can just burn away

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:17.970
What's right for me is for me alone

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:22.850
Whatever the path, I'll follow it to you

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:27.690
This feeling grows and grows,
deep inside my heart

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:31.150
For one single reason

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:39.120
I continue to climb up on the stage

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:53.510
#2 Promise

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:59.890
Hey there beautiful, you did a great job
beating up my puppet.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:03.640
But you're out of luck this time.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:09.650
Pulcinella's strength and construction
are in a completely different league.

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:14.610
I don't know if you're after
his money or what, but it ain't funny.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:15.610
Stand back.

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:18.120
-You keep out of this.
-What?

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:27.040
Where am I?

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:29.800
What happened to me?

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:34.260
Shirogane, Narumi!

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:39.560
I'll give you plenty of good oil
once you kill the boy, Pulcinella.

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:42.480
Our client will pay us heartily for that.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:45.690
Client? Who hired you?

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:48.020
Stand back. I'll protect Mr. Masaru.

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:50.150
By myself.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:55.860
How wonderful.
I usually only get to kill humans.

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:59.530
It'll be nice
to fight a puppet for a change.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:04.710
Here we go, one on one!

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:10.090
I see you're quick.

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:11.840
But take this!

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:17.010
Shirogane!

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:21.220
This punch has the force
to demolish concrete walls.

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:36.360
Impossible! What is this puppet?

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:39.740
Get back!

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:49.170
It can't move? Unbelievable.

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:52.590
Her puppet's holding Pulcinella down
with just one hand.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:55.050
You see, Mr. Masaru?

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:57.930
This is what
your grandfather's Arlequin can do.

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:01.930
Les Arts Martiaux!

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:09.980
Damn it. Defend yourself!

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:12.570
Swirling Tiger!

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:21.320
What the...
It's on a whole different level.

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:23.280
But...

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:25.370
Shirogane!

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:26.580
Mr. Masaru!

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:30.500
You... What a dirty trick!

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:37.210
Exactly.
We live in a dirty world, beautiful.

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:43.760
I assume it's obvious,
but one wrong move and...

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:48.180
I was too busy fighting
and didn't notice them.

00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:49.730
It's all my fault.

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:52.900
Sorry, but it's all a part of my job.

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:53.940
Do it.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:02.910
This ain't funny, you jerks.

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:04.200
-You...!
-Take this!

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:11.370
I'm out of luck today.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:12.790
We'll meet again.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:16.090
-Wait for us!
-Damn it!

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:19.170
You okay, Masaru?

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:25.260
I couldn't win. Not on my own.

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:30.140
What's going on... What happened here?

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:32.100
This is just...

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:34.690
You really banged this place up.

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:37.480
A man can't get a night's sleep here.

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:41.360
I'm sorry. It's all my fault.

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:45.830
The train, and now this hospital...

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:48.910
I mess up everything I touch.

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:51.790
But I don't know what to do...

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:55.710
Masaru. First up, stop crying.

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:56.920
And then, laugh.

00:05:57.550 --> 00:05:59.380
How could I laugh now?

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:02.930
You did nothing wrong. Besides...

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:07.010
if you don't laugh, I'll die.

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:10.060
What do you mean?

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:15.900
Physiological dysfunction caused by
third party parasympathetic dominance.

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:18.360
ZONAPHA syndrome...

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:21.530
Yeah, I got it too.

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:24.820
Just like my old Grandpops.

00:06:24.990 --> 00:06:25.820
A disease?

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:30.580
It's not contagious!

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.120
Miss.

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:37.840
Humans have a sympathetic nervous system
and a parasympathetic nervous system.

00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:43.130
When the parasympathetic nervous system
is dominant, people are relaxed.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:48.890
ZONAPHA syndrome is where the body
is affected by the parasympathetic nerves.

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:50.640
What do you mean?

00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:56.650
When the body senses that people close by
aren't relaxed, it causes an attack.

00:06:57.060 --> 00:07:02.650
When that happens, the trachea contracts,
causing breathing difficulties.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:05.450
Excruciating pain is felt in every nerve.

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:08.160
Damn it, it's starting.

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:11.700
What if you approach someone
who's already laughing?

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:14.910
No, that doesn't work for some reason.

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:19.670
I have to make them laugh.
Uh-oh, it's getting worse.

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:26.970
Is it funny?

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:28.760
Nah, sorry.

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:30.890
Miss?

00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:34.930
I've never been someone who laughs a lot.

00:07:36.190 --> 00:07:37.650
Bah, you guys are useless.

00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:41.730
I'm going out to make someone laugh.

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:44.740
Narumi!

00:07:44.990 --> 00:07:47.110
Leave him alone, Mr. Masaru.

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:51.330
But he's the one that saved us.

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:54.580
I might not be able to do much,

00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:57.620
but I want to help him in return.

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:07.470
Laugh...

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:10.180
Laugh...!

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:14.520
How's this? Will this make you laugh?

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:17.980
Then, how about this?

00:08:21.150 --> 00:08:23.820
Laugh! Don't run away!

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:26.280
Somebody, help!

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:31.490
Speak up. How can I make you laugh?

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:34.030
I'll do whatever you say.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:35.740
Come on!

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:37.040
Idiot!

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:40.290
How can they laugh
when you're scaring them?

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:44.250
She's right. I'd panicked from the pain.

00:08:44.840 --> 00:08:48.170
Mr. Masaru came looking for you
because he was worried.

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:49.680
You don't deserve it!

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:52.140
-But...
-No "buts"!

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:53.640
What's going on?

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:58.100
Maybe they're comedians,
putting on an impromptu act.

00:08:58.310 --> 00:09:00.230
Yeah, she's dressed weird.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:03.650
-But...
-No duck faces either.

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:08.150
All right, get him girl.

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:11.860
Come on, man.

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:14.450
That was close...

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:16.950
Good for you, Narumi.

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:19.080
You two are a perfect match.

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:22.170
I do not want to be
a perfect match with him.

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:24.460
Yeah, same here.

00:09:37.390 --> 00:09:38.430
Narumi.

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:41.640
I'm sorry you had to bring me here.

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:46.270
It's nothing. They might
come for you again if you go home.

00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:52.990
But jeez, who's behind all this anyways?

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:55.370
Do you think it could be a relative?

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:57.080
I don't know.

00:09:57.410 --> 00:10:00.700
I only became a part of the Saiga family
3 years ago.

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:03.790
I haven't met all my relatives.

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:07.840
3 years ago?
But you're Saiga's son, right?

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:13.930
But my mom was
what they call a "mistress."

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:18.140
Where did you learn that word?

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:23.940
I used to live alone with my mom
when I was little.

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:27.940
She used to work hard
for little money every day.

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:32.650
When she died,
a lawyer came to take me away.

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:34.660
That's when I first met Dad.

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:38.740
The Saiga family took me in after that.

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:44.830
Hey, Narumi?

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:48.420
How much does a proper grave cost?

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:51.170
Huh? I don't really know.

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:55.720
I wasn't at all interested
in the inheritance.

00:10:56.970 --> 00:11:00.350
I just wanted...

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:03.180
to build Mom a grave.

00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:10.360
What's wrong, Narumi?

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:12.110
Nothing.

00:11:12.780 --> 00:11:14.070
Here you are.

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:18.950
Damn it.

00:11:19.370 --> 00:11:24.750
How am I supposed to act around him
after hearing that?

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:29.540
Eat up, Masaru.

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:31.800
Fix those wounds with nutrition.

00:11:32.130 --> 00:11:35.420
Eat your vegetables too.
Here, I cut your casserole.

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:37.260
You got some here.

00:11:37.510 --> 00:11:40.050
Stop. He can't eat in peace like that.

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:43.140
I will care for him. You shut up.

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:48.980
I've figured out Masaru, but her...

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:54.360
She calls herself Shirogane,
but is that even her real name?

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:59.780
She said she'd protect Masaru,
but who knows what she's really after?

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:04.080
It was delicious. Thank you, Shirogane.

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:07.580
Really? Oh thank you!

00:12:12.420 --> 00:12:14.460
Dang, she's pretty.

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:20.390
I hate her guts, but she looks beautiful
when she's taking care of Masaru.

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:22.850
Fine, I'll give her that.

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:28.810
Whatever her deal is,
one thing for sure is she's hot.

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:37.110
A lot happened today.

00:12:38.950 --> 00:12:43.910
Though I bet nobody at
the Saiga household is worrying about me.

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:50.710
Shirogane?

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:53.840
You must be having trouble
washing yourself.

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:55.500
Let me help you.

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:58.010
Wait, no! I'm fine!

00:12:58.170 --> 00:12:59.760
Oh yeah.

00:12:59.970 --> 00:13:02.340
He can't wash himself with that arm.

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:06.890
Hey Masaru. Let me wash your back...

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:15.110
No, I, I just...

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:18.030
I didn't think you'd be in here.

00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:20.740
Am I being a busybody?

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:32.420
Damn it.

00:13:39.010 --> 00:13:41.880
Getting all distracted over nothing.

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:44.430
Come on, concentrate.

00:13:44.590 --> 00:13:45.800
Narumi.

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:48.310
Is that a martial art?

00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:51.730
Yeah, I learned it when I was in China.

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:53.520
Wow, in China?

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:57.900
You grab the opponent's arm
and hit the face.

00:13:58.280 --> 00:14:00.780
Then, you step in and go for the leg.

00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:03.820
Impressed?

00:14:03.990 --> 00:14:08.740
Wow. I wish I were strong like you.

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:14.670
Then I wouldn't be so scared to death
like I am now.

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:17.960
Listen here, Masaru.

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:20.340
It's the same for me.

00:14:20.510 --> 00:14:25.010
I was scared too when I fought
those puppets and bad guys.

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:29.220
But how can you fight
when you're scared like that?

00:14:32.980 --> 00:14:36.610
I don't know. I just wanted to.

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:41.030
But hey, I know how you feel.

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:46.320
I was a weakling like you as a kid.
I was bullied all the time.

00:14:46.910 --> 00:14:49.990
Really? You were like me?

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:54.290
Then could I become strong like you?

00:14:58.840 --> 00:15:01.760
That's what I've always wanted.

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:07.640
To be strong.

00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:14.230
If I were stronger, they'd listen to me.

00:15:15.480 --> 00:15:21.070
If I were stronger,
I'd be able to smile all the time.

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:31.700
An album?

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:36.580
Yeah, I was going to burn it,
but you can take a look.

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:40.130
But don't tell anybody.
It's bloody embarrassing.

00:15:43.760 --> 00:15:45.130
This is you?

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:46.880
Y-Yeah...

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:50.390
This is me crying,
not wanting to go to school.

00:15:50.890 --> 00:15:53.640
This is me crying because I hated milk.

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:57.390
And the sports festival.
I finished last, of course.

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:02.610
There, you laughed.

00:16:04.030 --> 00:16:07.110
You're the only one
I can make laugh for now.

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:11.410
You need to keep laughing for me
so I don't die.

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:13.910
Want to give it a shot?

00:16:14.290 --> 00:16:16.000
Really? You'll teach me?

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:20.670
But I'm weak and clumsy.
I'm no good at PE.

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:24.840
You dork, you saw the pictures.
I was scrawny too.

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:27.550
But I wanted to become strong.

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:29.930
You and I are alike.

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:34.680
You mean, I can become strong like you?

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:38.600
Yeah, even stronger than me.

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:43.610
There you are, Mr. Masaru.

00:16:44.730 --> 00:16:46.400
I borrowed your shirt.

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:53.410
Fine. Whatever.

00:16:53.580 --> 00:16:55.620
Sorry for what happened back there.

00:16:56.040 --> 00:16:57.160
What about it?

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:59.870
It happens all the time at the circus.

00:17:00.670 --> 00:17:02.540
Did you think I'd care?

00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:06.300
But you know,
I'd rather have you forget about it.

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:10.680
You must be tired, Mr. Masaru.
Time to get some sleep.

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:13.850
-Yeah, yeah.
-Um, Narumi?

00:17:14.390 --> 00:17:17.100
Will you stay with me
until I become strong?

00:17:17.810 --> 00:17:20.690
Will you stay and
not leave me like Mom did?

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:22.190
Sure thing!

00:17:24.940 --> 00:17:26.690
Why'd I say that?

00:17:27.230 --> 00:17:29.950
He and I live in different worlds.

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:32.780
Who am I to encourage him like that?

00:17:32.950 --> 00:17:35.490
Learn martial arts? Yeah, right.

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:42.670
But I'd hate to be separated from him.

00:17:56.600 --> 00:17:57.680
Bathroom...

00:17:58.100 --> 00:17:59.640
I'll go with you.

00:18:00.270 --> 00:18:01.520
No, I'm fine!

00:18:05.690 --> 00:18:08.480
I wonder if she isn't sleepy.

00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:18.740
Mr. Masaru!

00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:23.540
It's so easy
to kidnap a single little brat.

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:25.750
S-Shirogane...

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:29.380
Damn it, Arlequin is in the other room!

00:18:30.090 --> 00:18:31.550
Let go of Mr. Masaru!

00:18:34.220 --> 00:18:35.050
Shirogane!

00:18:36.760 --> 00:18:37.930
Masaru!

00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:43.140
-Narumi!
-I'm coming for you!

00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:51.230
Amateurs are so easy to put out.

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:53.860
Come on. There's no time to play around.

00:18:54.650 --> 00:18:57.490
-Narumi! Shirogane!
-Mr. Masaru!

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:11.800
Damn it. Call the cops.

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:13.010
Forget it.

00:19:16.260 --> 00:19:19.970
Calling the cops
will just take you more time.

00:19:20.140 --> 00:19:21.390
You...!

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:25.690
How dare you!
You're with the kidnappers!

00:19:25.980 --> 00:19:29.520
Who are you?
Where did you take Mr. Masaru?

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:33.570
You sure are as hot as ever.

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:36.200
Hey, easy now.

00:19:36.450 --> 00:19:41.280
We're not the ones that kidnapped the boy.
They're more like our rivals.

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:43.620
What the hell does that mean?

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:44.950
Speak.

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:48.500
First, let me introduce myself.

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:51.670
I'm Eiryo Ashihana.

00:19:51.840 --> 00:19:55.550
You know the situation
concerning that boy, right?

00:19:56.090 --> 00:20:02.640
It all started when the boy inherited
the entire Saiga fortune.

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:06.020
There're certain people
who don't like it.

00:20:06.480 --> 00:20:10.610
We're the Slaughter Team,
hired to kill the boy.

00:20:11.440 --> 00:20:15.400
You're serious?
You were really going to kill a kid?

00:20:16.110 --> 00:20:18.490
Sure, that's how we earn our living.

00:20:18.990 --> 00:20:20.070
You bastard!

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:22.490
Then who kidnapped Mr. Masaru?

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:25.370
They're the Kidnap Team.

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:30.170
We're the Slaughter Team,
hired to kill the boy.

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:34.880
And they're the Kidnap Team,
hired to kidnap the boy.

00:20:35.300 --> 00:20:37.380
We're hired by different people.

00:20:38.300 --> 00:20:40.180
You know them?

00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:44.260
Of course. We're all of the same family.

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:46.310
Funny, eh?

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:52.020
We puppeteers have split into 2 factions
and are trying to outwit each other.

00:20:52.400 --> 00:20:53.820
Who hired the Kidnap Team?

00:20:54.940 --> 00:20:59.030
Let's just say, a certain somebody
who wants to adopt the boy.

00:20:59.610 --> 00:21:03.410
The boy is being taken to
the Saiga villa in Karuizawa.

00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:07.450
I tried to stop them by crashing into them
but failed.

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:11.710
I'm heading over there now,
but how about you?

00:21:12.210 --> 00:21:13.290
Do we have a choice?

00:21:13.460 --> 00:21:17.210
Oh yes, let me tell you one last thing.

00:21:18.470 --> 00:21:23.390
That villa is a Karakuri mansion,
full of the late Saiga's heinous puppets.

00:21:23.680 --> 00:21:28.560
Plus, it's protected by the family's
most seasoned puppeteers.

00:21:29.520 --> 00:21:33.270
I exist to protect Mr. Masaru
and nothing else.

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:36.690
Shame on you, all you people!

00:21:37.190 --> 00:21:40.280
Trying to kidnap and kill
a young innocent child.

00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:44.530
He's doing his best to live
like any other boy!

00:21:45.030 --> 00:21:48.330
Wait for me Masaru, I'll save you.

00:21:52.670 --> 00:21:58.250
In my heart, I kept praying
Shirogane and Narumi would come.

00:21:59.260 --> 00:22:03.840
But I didn't know back then,

00:22:04.640 --> 00:22:09.520
that it was only the beginning
of the fear that was closing in on me.

00:22:14.730 --> 00:22:17.110
Fly up high, Marionette

00:22:17.270 --> 00:22:19.360
Turn to ash, gracefully

00:22:19.530 --> 00:22:23.910
My only purpose in life was to fight

00:22:24.110 --> 00:22:28.740
Why am I so angry
even I dump my humanity

00:22:28.910 --> 00:22:35.040
Without you, I can't smile anymore

00:22:36.080 --> 00:22:40.260
I assume that I am to be blamed

00:22:40.420 --> 00:22:44.720
Like a puppet that can't smile naturally

00:22:44.880 --> 00:22:49.890
I feel like someone is pulling my strings

00:22:50.100 --> 00:22:53.640
What am I even living for?

00:22:53.810 --> 00:22:58.150
I was hurt, and thought
that nobody would understand

00:22:58.310 --> 00:23:03.190
But you came along,
and took me in your arms

00:23:03.360 --> 00:23:09.240
I felt my tangled arms and legs

00:23:09.620 --> 00:23:11.620
become free

00:23:11.950 --> 00:23:14.250
Fly up high, Marionette

00:23:14.410 --> 00:23:16.580
I think now I can reach you

00:23:16.750 --> 00:23:21.130
Before I met you, I was empty

00:23:21.300 --> 00:23:25.880
Now I have something
I'd give my all to protect

00:23:26.050 --> 00:23:32.430
You taught me how to feel,
the feeling of sorrow too
